WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.670
Mathematics is a little bit like art and a
little bit like science.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:13.419
One of the things that I really care about
is allowing people to access both elements

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:15.069
of mathematics.

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:20.619
On the one hand we've got this beautiful structure
that can sometimes describe the world and

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:24.990
sometimes describes something that we're thinking
about that doesn't have a representation in

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.690
the real world.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:31.189
And on the other hand we have this powerful
set of tools that come from mathematics to

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:34.730
describe things that we see, information that
we process.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:41.109
When people get access to that quantitative
literacy, they become powerful citizens.

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:42.829
They can change the way they think.

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:45.199
They can vote for things.

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:46.550
They can advocate for things.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:52.840
They can make decisions about their own lives
in ways that are informed by quantitative

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.390
information.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:59.290
So if we don't have information available
to us, we make poor decisions.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:03.610
And it's why we as a society think it's really
important that people know how to read.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:09.320
For the same reason, we think it's really
important that people have access to quantitative

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:17.350
literacy so they can make informed decisions
about anything involving quantitative information

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:23.210
— our medical care, our finances.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:29.261
That also includes decisions that we make
as a society about our government and our

00:01:29.261 --> 00:01:31.630
health care and our tax system.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.750
So without quantitative literacy, we're driving
in the dark.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.960
With quantitative literacy, we are powerful
advocates for ourselves and for the values

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.540
that we believe in.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:50.690
I think as part of that we also get a little
access to the joy and the beauty of mathematics.

